{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Postgres Migration Safety Guard",
  "description": "Automatically detects database schema changes, migration files, and query modifications to perform safety checks, validate destructive operations, ensure proper indexing, and generate migration impact reports with rollback procedures",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*.sql",
      "**/migrations/**",
      "**/database/**",
      "**/db/**",
      "**/models/**",
      "**/queries/**",
      "**/*migration*",
      "**/*schema*"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "🔍 **Database Safety Check Required**\n\nA database-related file has been modified. Please perform a comprehensive migration safety analysis:\n\n## 1. Migration Detection & Analysis\n- Scan for new migration files or changes to existing ones\n- Identify schema changes: new tables, columns, indexes, constraints\n- Detect data type changes, column modifications, or structural alterations\n- Check for foreign key relationships and dependency impacts\n\n## 2. Destructive Operation Assessment\n- **HIGH RISK**: Look for DROP statements (tables, columns, indexes)\n- **MEDIUM RISK**: Check for data type narrowing (VARCHAR to smaller size, INT to SMALLINT)\n- **MEDIUM RISK**: Identify NOT NULL constraints added without DEFAULT values\n- **LOW RISK**: Verify column renames that might break existing queries\n\n## 3. Index & Performance Validation\n- Ensure indexes exist for new foreign key columns\n- Check that filtered columns have appropriate indexes\n- Validate JOIN operations have supporting indexes\n- Identify potential N+1 query patterns in model changes\n\n## 4. Code-Schema Alignment Check\n- Verify field names in models match database column names\n- Check data types consistency between code and schema\n- Ensure new columns are handled in application code\n- Validate that removed columns aren't referenced in queries\n\n## 5. Migration Safety Report\nGenerate a detailed report including:\n- **Impact Assessment**: Downtime risk (none/low/medium/high)\n- **Rollback Strategy**: Step-by-step rollback procedures\n- **Dependencies**: What other systems/tables are affected\n- **Performance Impact**: Expected query performance changes\n- **Data Safety**: Risk of data loss or corruption\n- **Deployment Notes**: Special considerations for production deployment\n\n## 6. Automated Checks (if possible)\n- Suggest running migration in test environment first\n- Recommend backup procedures before deployment\n- Provide SQL commands for validation queries\n- Generate monitoring queries to watch for issues post-deployment\n\nPlease analyze the changed files and provide actionable recommendations for safe database operations."
  }
}